    A15_SMSS_71_M016935_031                                                   
                                                                              
    Apollo 15 Soil Mechanics                                                  
    Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page E-1                         
                                                                              
    Plot of Pre-Flight Load Calibration tests                                 
                                                                              
    This handdrawn plot shows the drum circumferential deflection in          
    millimeters versus the load in Newtons for PDA/drum S/N 2005 of the       
    Apollo 15 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) flight unit. A series  
    of 12 calibration tests were run, the point at the upper right has a      
    note, "spring bottomed out, ignore this point", The other 11 points form  
    a straight line. Thinner lines are plotted alongside this line            
    representing the 2 sigma uncertainty in the calibration curve.  The load  
    in Newtons (ordinate) is labelled from 0 to 100 newtons, and the drum     
    circumferential deflection (abscissa) is labelled from 0 to 15            
    millimeters. The test was done at U.C. Berkeley on 25 June 1971.  Note    
    that this test is for "PDSA/DRUM S/N 2005", the lunar drum used on        
    Apollo 15 was S/N 2002.                                                   
                                                                              
